<tr id="mwsA">
<td align="center" id="mwsQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1950_NBA_Finals" title="1950 NBA Finals" about="#mwt44" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwsg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nbafy","href":"./Template:Nbafy"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"1950"}},"i":0}}]}'>1950</a></td><td style="background:#FFFF99" id="mwsw"><b id="mwtA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1949–50_Minneapolis_Lakers_season" title="1949–50 Minneapolis Lakers season" id="mwtQ">Minneapolis Lakers</a> (1)</b> <sup about="#mwt45" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-14"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#tag:ref","function":"tag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Minneapolis was the Central Division (now defunct, no relation to the current [[Central Division (NBA)|Central Division]]) playoff champion, while the [[Anderson Packers]] were the Western Division playoff champion.&lt;ref name=globegazette /> Due to the NBA&apos;s realignment into three divisions,&lt;ref>{{cite web |title=Season Review: 1949–50 |date=April 24, 2017 |website=NBA.com |url=https://www.nba.com/history/season-recap/1949-50|access-date=May 16, 2019|archive-date=April 13, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190413185332/https://www.nba.com/history/season-recap/1949-50|url-status=live}}&lt;/ref>&lt;ref>{{cite book |last1=Hollander |first1=Zander |last2=Sachare |first2=Alex |title=The Official NBA Basketball Encyclopedia |year=1989 |publisher=Villard Books |pages=[https://archive.org/details/officialnbabaske00holl/page/49 49]–51 |url=https://archive.org/details/officialnbabaske00holl|url-access=registration |isbn=0-394-58039-7|access-date=May 16, 2019}}&lt;/ref> the team with the best regular season record after the divisional finals advanced automatically to the NBA Finals, while the other two teams faced off in the NBA semifinals to determine the other finalist. Eastern Division playoff champion Syracuse had the best regular season record among the division playoff champions, causing Minneapolis to face Anderson in the NBA semifinals.&lt;ref name=globegazette>{{cite news |title=Anderson, Lakers Play for Shot at Syracuse Nationals |date=April 3, 1950 |newspaper=Mason City Globe Gazette |page=11 |url=https://www.newspapers.com/clip/29442218/ski_73/ |via=[[Newspapers.com]]|access-date=May 16, 2019|archive-date=July 14, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190714194656/https://www.newspapers.com/clip/29442218/ski_73/|url-status=live}}&lt;/ref>&lt;ref name=\"Minneapolis Lakers\" />"},"2":{"wt":"group=lower-alpha"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-14" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwtg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuA">[</span>b<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuQ">]</span></span></a></sup> <small id="mwug">(2, 2–0)</small></td><td align="center" id="mwuw">4–2</td><td id="mwvA"><i id="mwvQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1949–50_Syracuse_Nationals_season" title="1949–50 Syracuse Nationals season" id="mwvg">Syracuse Nationals</a></i> (1) <small id="mwvw">(1, 0–1)</small></td><td id="mwwA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Cervi" title="Al Cervi" id="mwwQ">Al Cervi</a></td>
<td align="center" id="mwwg"><sup about="#mwt77" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Minneapolis_Lakers_13-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Minneapolis Lakers"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Minneapolis_Lakers-13"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Minneapolis_Lakers-13" id="mwww"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwxA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxQ">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt80" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-15"}}'><a href="#cite_note-15" id="mwxw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwyA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyQ">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyg">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr>
